  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Exam Paper",
    "overview": "Every surface speaks the language of the NMT answer sheet (бланк відповідей): printed numbered cells on cool paper, filled in ballpoint ink. This is a sheet you fill in calmly, not a quiz game. Colour is scarce and always means something: ink is the student's mark, and red, amber and green are states, never decoration.\n\nThe world has two densities. The student surface is phone-first and roomy: large targets, an 18px prompt, one question at a time, nothing moving. The teacher surface is desktop-first and dense: a hairline-ruled table that reads a whole class at a glance, with rows needing action sorted to the top.\n\nUI text is Ukrainian throughout. Numbers (timer, counts, cell numbers, times) always use tabular numerals.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cool paper-white ground, graphite text, never cream.",
      "One ballpoint-ink blue accent, for \"your mark\" and the primary action only.",
